  "details": "Reproduced in VRChat for Windows; build id `1159`.\nI tried adjusting the `cache_expiry_delay` by creating a config file as documented on https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/configuration-file#size-and-expiry-time\nThe documentation states that `cache_expiry_delay` can be set to values `Greater than or equal to 30`\nWhen launching VRChat with `cache_expiry_delay` set to a value >150 the following line gets printed to the ouput log text file:\n`Error - Cache expiration may not be higher then 12960000`\nThis came unexpected for me as the documentation appears to be clear on this and i expected this value to be limited by more technical aspects like timestamp range, integer limits or whatever. I only noticed this coincidentally.\nPlease update the documentation to reflect this or drop this limitation if possible.",
